    "title": "Rep. Brenden Jones questions UNC Chapel Hill spending on LGBTQ+ programs - South Raleigh News",
    "text": "Rep. Brenden Jones, a Republican representing North Carolina’s 46th House district since 2017, raised questions on social media regarding the funding and programming for LGBTQ+ students at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill.\nOn September 16, 2025, Jones posted: “I just discovered that every year UNC has what’s called “Lavender Graduation”, which is a specific graduation for only LQBTQ+ students and their “allies.” Is this a good use of NC taxpayer money? #ncpol https://t.co/5eGLinTsBc”\nLater that day, he shared a second post containing only a link: “https://t.co/tcIGcR1k3n” (September 16, 2025).\nThe following day, Jones highlighted staff salaries at the university’s LGBT Center: “UNC Chapel Hill spends $222,650 dollars a year in staff salaries for the UNC Chapel Hill LGBT Center. Director: $108,150 Assistant Director: $70,000 Admin Support Specialist: $44,500 Should your tax dollars fund this? #ncpol https://t.co/eb466zSrW4” (September 17, 2025).\nJones has represented his district in the North Carolina State House since replacing Ken Waddell in 2017.",
